WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.522
The boys watched as the man crossed the street.

2
00:00:03.523 --> 00:00:07.670
"We have to follow him," Bobby almost shouted.

3
00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:12.039
"Maybe we should find the police," Cy said uncertainly.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.362
"We don't have time. Come on!"

5
00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:17.828
Bobby made sure the street was clear.

6
00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:20.659
Then he ran over to the other side.

7
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.685
His brother followed him.

8
00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:24.443
The man walked quickly.

9
00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:26.576
He kept looking at his watch.

10
00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:30.130
"He must be meeting someone," Bobby said.

11
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:34.535
Hiding behind a car, the boys watched the man.

12
00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:37.001
He stopped in front of a dark van.

13
00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:38.376
The window opened.

14
00:00:38.377 --> 00:00:42.708
Another man with a ponytail was inside.

15
00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:47.525
Bobby pointed and exclaimed, "He's getting into that van!"

16
00:00:47.526 --> 00:00:49.352
"What's the license plate?"

17
00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:51.837
Cy searched for the numbers.

18
00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:55.499
The van started its engine and sped down the street.

19
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.521
"I memorized the numbers," Cy said.

20
00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:01.211
"Let's go find the police."

21
00:01:01.212 --> 00:01:05.580
The boys ran and ran until they found an officer.

22
00:01:05.581 --> 00:01:08.575
"Officer!" they shouted.

23
00:01:08.576 --> 00:01:12.541
"Where's the fire, boys?" the policeman laughed.

24
00:01:12.542 --> 00:01:15.641
Cy and Bobby explained what they'd seen.

25
00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.197
The officer stopped laughing.

26
00:01:18.198 --> 00:01:21.712
He looked very serious as he wrote down the numbers.

27
00:01:21.713 --> 00:01:24.997
"Thanks for your help," the officer said.

28
00:01:24.998 --> 00:01:27.423
Then the boys headed back home.

29
00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:29.434
"What took so long?"

30
00:01:29.435 --> 00:01:32.928
Aunt Martha said as she took the bread from Cy.

31
00:01:32.929 --> 00:01:35.663
The boys explained what had happened.

32
00:01:35.664 --> 00:01:38.410
The townspeople listened too.

33
00:01:38.411 --> 00:01:42.836
Not long after, Panther walked into the kitchen with a police officer.

34
00:01:42.837 --> 00:01:45.999
It was the same one the boys had spoken to.

35
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.263
"The bank robbers have been caught," he announced.

36
00:01:49.264 --> 00:01:51.377
Everyone cheered loudly.

37
00:01:51.378 --> 00:01:53.260
"You can thank the boys,"

38
00:01:53.261 --> 00:01:56.459
the officer said, patting them on the back.

39
00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.757
Cy and Bobby turned red.

40
00:01:58.758 --> 00:02:01.097
Their neighbors shook their hands.

41
00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:03.361
They gave them hugs.

42
00:02:03.362 --> 00:02:07.071
"I'm so proud of you," cried Aunt Martha.

43
00:02:07.072 --> 00:02:11.175
When everyone had left, the children flopped onto the sofa.

44
00:02:11.176 --> 00:02:13.783
Outside it was getting dark.

45
00:02:13.784 --> 00:02:18.215
"I guess people here aren't that bad," said Panther.

46
00:02:18.216 --> 00:02:25.019
"But after the sun sets, they'll forget what happened," Bobby said in a sad voice.

47
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.529
"They'll forget all about us," Cy added.

48
00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:33.490
"At least we know people can be nice," Jane said.

49
00:02:33.491 --> 00:02:36.422
The children watched as the sun disappeared.

50
00:02:36.423 --> 00:02:39.845
A sharp knock on the door startled them.

51
00:02:39.846 --> 00:02:41.515
Cy opened the door.

52
00:02:41.516 --> 00:02:43.417
It was Farmer Jenkins.

53
00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:48.872
"I brought some homemade jam for our heroes," he said, smiling.

54
00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:52.174
"Huh?" Bobby was confused.

55
00:02:52.175 --> 00:02:55.559
"What for?" asked Panther cautiously.

56
00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.030
She still remembered how much jam they owed Farmer Jenkins.

57
00:03:00.031 --> 00:03:04.795
"For helping to catch the robbers," the farmer chuckled.

58
00:03:04.796 --> 00:03:07.833
"I hope you kids enjoy this."

59
00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:11.806
He handed the jars to Cy then waved good-bye.

60
00:03:11.807 --> 00:03:15.341
The children looked at the jam guiltily.

61
00:03:15.342 --> 00:03:18.177
"Why did he remember the robbery?"

62
00:03:18.178 --> 00:03:22.104
Bobby was still confused, looking outside at the dark.

63
00:03:22.105 --> 00:03:26.925
"Huey said everything returns to normal once the sun sets."

64
00:03:26.926 --> 00:03:29.397
No one could explain it.

65
00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:33.175
Early the next morning, the children went to see Huey.

66
00:03:33.176 --> 00:03:38.141
As soon as Cy pulled him up, Bobby started to throw out questions.

67
00:03:38.142 --> 00:03:42.058
"Whoa!" Huey held up his hand.

68
00:03:42.059 --> 00:03:45.282
"What exactly was your wish again?"

69
00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:49.103
"For something exciting to happen," answered Bobby.

70
00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:52.303
"And did it?" Huey asked.

71
00:03:52.304 --> 00:03:55.589
"There was a bank robbery," said Bobby.

72
00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:59.244
"It was more kind of scary than exciting."

73
00:03:59.245 --> 00:04:03.573
"What else happened?" Huey asked.

74
00:04:03.574 --> 00:04:07.377
"We got to meet many new people," said Cy.

75
00:04:07.378 --> 00:04:13.013
"So maybe the bank robbery wasn't the wish," said Huey.

76
00:04:13.014 --> 00:04:16.537
"I don't understand," said Bobby.

77
00:04:16.538 --> 00:04:21.178
"How did it feel to meet new people?" asked Huey.

78
00:04:21.179 --> 00:04:23.650
The children were thoughtful.

79
00:04:23.651 --> 00:04:25.421
Finally Bobby answered.

80
00:04:25.422 --> 00:04:28.805
"It was kind of exciting," he said.

81
00:04:28.806 --> 00:04:31.871
"Maybe that was your wish."

82
00:04:31.872 --> 00:04:34.858
Huey spread his hands like a magician.

83
00:04:34.859 --> 00:04:38.640
"But the wish ended yesterday," said Jane.

84
00:04:38.641 --> 00:04:41.390
"Will they stop being our friends now?"

85
00:04:41.391 --> 00:04:47.390
"That depends on you," said Huey.

